  "description": "OCOSIK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C98 H93 Dy7 N6 O40,2(C1 H4 O1),4.25(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.564-4.014 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.49-117.42°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C100H109.5Dy7N6O46.25. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 5 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
